# Banned-name list — copy to .acstack-banned (gitignored) and edit.
#
# scripts/check.sh fails the guard if any of these appear in pack content.
# One extended-regex alternative per line; blank lines and # comments are
# ignored. Matching is word-boundary and case-insensitive.
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS NOT THE LIST ITSELF: the list names the very clients,
# collaborators, and projects you are trying to keep out of a public repo.
# Committing it publishes exactly what it exists to protect — and until
# 2026-07-29 this pack made that mistake, hardcoding a real roster inside
# check.sh, which also did not scan its own directory and so could never
# catch itself. Keep your real list untracked.
#
# Pick tokens that are distinctive. Short common words — a bare first
# name, a three-letter fragment — will false-positive on ordinary prose,
# so prefer a full surname or a distinctive codename. (This file once
# used two entries from a real roster to illustrate that point, which is
# the same mistake one directory over.)

acmecorp
initech
globex
some-client-project
